 "DAY": "<ul>\n<li><b>1. Book</b> a licence-conversion (外免切替) slot at the licence centre of the prefecture where you are registered.</li>\n<li><b>2. Document screening.</b> They check the licence, translation, juminhyo and the 3-month stay. This can take hours.</li>\n<li><b>3. Aptitude test.</b> Vision and colour recognition (red, yellow, blue).</li>\n<li><b>4. Knowledge test.</b> 50 true/false questions in text only, 45 to pass. English and around 20 other languages are offered — confirm with your centre.</li>\n<li><b>5. Practical test</b> on the centre's closed course, usually on a later day. 70 points to pass.</li>\n<li><b>6. Pass.</b> Pay the issuance fee and receive the licence.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"muted\">Licences from some countries and regions (many European countries, Australia, New Zealand, Canada, South Korea, Taiwan and a few US states, among others) are exempt from the knowledge and practical tests. Everyone else takes both. Check your prefectural police website for the current list.</p>",
